rngb is an unofficial native R parser for NETZSCH STA NGB files.

The binary grammar, table model, channel mappings and metadata extraction
rules were adapted from pyngb by Grayson Bellamy, under the MIT License.
Reference: https://github.com/GraysonBellamy/pyngb
Pinned source commit: 3650627ebabbdf41d4ce70310b0fd036bb0f9f85 (version 0.6.0).
The R implementation is independently executed and requires no Python.

